preConditionHook:
// THE DOUBLE BOTTOM FAILS -- entry WITH the break. A double bottom bull flag
// sets up, the market immediately reverses instead, and price falls breakTicks
// below the pattern's level: traders sell on a stop one tick below, looking
// for a downside measured move. The long mirror is the break ABOVE a double
// top.
//
// SIDES. The book states the setup as a SELL (the bull pattern failing), so
// the bullish reading -- the break above a double top -- is this rule's LONG
// side and the passage's own trade is the short. That is the corpus's
// mirroring convention, not a change of meaning.
//
// patternWindow IS THE FAILURE WINDOW, not the pivot window: the pattern's
// second pivot must have confirmed no more than patternWindow bars ago, which
// is R12-05's "immediately reverses" (stated as three bars, carried at five).
// pivotLookback is the window the pivots themselves are sought in, and
// matchTicks the tolerance that makes two extremes "the same price"; both ARE
// PROMOTED, as the merged parameters name neither. The pattern and its level
// are spelled exactly as in DoubleExtremePullback and DoubleExtremeDipBreakout
// -- the two most recent confirmed swing lows within matchTicks of each other,
// the LEVEL being the LOWER of them (the higher of the two highs for a double
// top), which is the price a breakout has to clear. Ticks division-first,
// ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale() computed once into tickSz; both are
// per-symbol constants (VERIFIED).
//
// ONLY THE WITH-THE-BREAK FORM IS WRITTEN. The other failure Brooks describes
// -- price breaks beyond the pattern and closes back inside within a few
// bars, the third push of a wedge -- is FailedBreakoutBeyondExtreme applied to
// this level, and composes once that rule can take a supplied level. Whether
// the entry is with the break or against it is the whole difference between
// the two trades, so they stay apart.
//
// PIVOT SCAN inlined from SwingHigh.json per the B-list decision, occurrences
// 1 and 2 only (occurrence 3+ is unmeasured). MEASURED (EL_Swing_Probe.txt,
// @ES 60 min): the pivot bar is AT OR ABOVE the `strength` OLDER bars and
// STRICTLY ABOVE the `strength` NEWER bars -- bars-ago indexing, so the newer
// bars are the smaller k and take el_gt / el_lt, the older el_ge / el_le;
// confirmation lag exactly `strength`; candidate offsets
// strength..pivotLookback-1, the neighbourhood reaching `strength` bars past
// the window, so the deepest bar touched is pivotLookback - 1 + strength. The
// comparisons carry the 2.22e-12 relational tolerance. A flat run of equal
// lows is ONE pivot, not N. The -1 sentinel is guarded on both bar indices.
//
// Not DoubleExtremeDipBreakout, whose trigger is the extreme BETWEEN the two
// pivots -- a much further price -- rather than the pattern's own level. Not
// MicroDoubleExtreme (two bar extremes at a fixed small lag) and not Ledge
// (bars matching the current bar's extreme inside a window).
// Scratch below is declared in localVariables, not at hook scope: the
// generator only prefixes declared locals, so a hook-scope declaration
// is a redefinition when this rule is placed twice in one strategy.
// Every one is fully assigned each bar before it is read.
tickSz = ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale();
pivS = (int)strength;
pivW = (int)pivotLookback;
nHi = 0;
nLo = 0;
hiPx1 = -1.0;
hiBar1 = -1.0;
hiPx2 = -1.0;
hiBar2 = -1.0;
loPx1 = -1.0;
loBar1 = -1.0;
loPx2 = -1.0;
loBar2 = -1.0;
for (int j = pivS; j <= pivW - 1; ++j) {
    bool okHi = true;
    bool okLo = true;
    for (int k = j - pivS; k < j; ++k) {
        if (!el_gt(high[j], high[k])) okHi = false;
        if (!el_lt(low[j], low[k])) okLo = false;
    }
    for (int k = j + 1; k <= j + pivS; ++k) {
        if (!el_ge(high[j], high[k])) okHi = false;
        if (!el_le(low[j], low[k])) okLo = false;
    }
    if (okHi && nHi < 2) {
        nHi = nHi + 1;
        if (nHi == 1) { hiPx1 = high[j]; hiBar1 = (double)j; }
        if (nHi == 2) { hiPx2 = high[j]; hiBar2 = (double)j; }
    }
    if (okLo && nLo < 2) {
        nLo = nLo + 1;
        if (nLo == 1) { loPx1 = low[j]; loBar1 = (double)j; }
        if (nLo == 2) { loPx2 = low[j]; loBar2 = (double)j; }
    }
}
haveDb = (loBar1 != -1.0) && (loBar2 != -1.0) && el_le(loBar1, patternWindow)
    && el_le(std::fabs(loPx1 - loPx2), matchTicks * tickSz);
haveDt = (hiBar1 != -1.0) && (hiBar2 != -1.0) && el_le(hiBar1, patternWindow)
    && el_le(std::fabs(hiPx1 - hiPx2), matchTicks * tickSz);
dbLevel = loPx1;
if (el_lt(loPx2, loPx1)) dbLevel = loPx2;
dtLevel = hiPx1;
if (el_gt(hiPx2, hiPx1)) dtLevel = hiPx2;
